// markdownlint configuration for `docs/adr/` only. markdownlint-cli2 reads the config nearest each
// linted file, so this applies to the ADRs and to nothing else in the repository.
{
  // MD040 (fenced-code-language) is OFF here, deliberately, because these records fence MEASURED
  // OUTPUT far more often than source: at the time of writing 51 of the 78 fence lines under
  // docs/adr/ are bare, against 21 `csharp` and a handful of `xml`/`json`/`mermaid`. (It said
  // "43 of the 70" until ADR-0043; the ratio is the durable part, the integers drift with every
  // record added, so read them as of a commit rather than as a rule.)
  //
  // It is off rather than satisfied with `text` because the house rule runs the other way, and a
  // review has now asked for each direction in turn: on PR #94 the guidance was "use a bare fence
  // for the measured output — this block contains plain output, not source code, remove the `text`
  // info string"; on PR #96 the same linter asked to add it back. Both cannot be right, and the
  // bare form is what the corpus already does.
  //
  // Encoding it here is the point. The convention existed only as tribal knowledge, so every ADR
  // that pasted a terminal transcript cost a review round to re-settle. A rule a tool cannot read
  // is a rule that gets re-litigated.
  "MD040": false
}
